From 35f941d0f66232626938a6ec9f7f7cf4708d4a0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahriar Iravanian <siravan@svtsim.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:58:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] rusticol: the GPU recurrence runner zeroes and reduces
 the amplitudes

- The amplitude planes the runtime clears before a plan run are recorded
  (execute_direct_tile_rows_impl) and zeroed on the device instead of
  uploaded; the record is dropped when the plan run returns.
- The LC replay (run_replay_color_view_into_unprofiled and its profiled
  twin) asks the plan run to keep the amplitudes on the device and, when
  it did, hands the runner the selected amplitude planes with their
  weights: pacman_recurrence_v1_reduce adds weight * |A|^2 into the tile's
  per-point output in the same order and arithmetic
  (accumulate_lc_diagonal_amplitude), so 8 bytes per point come back
  instead of every amplitude. Without a library that can reduce, or when
  the plan run stays on the CPU, nothing changes.

u u~ > Z + 6g, 16,000 points, all flows and helicities, RTX 5060:
evaluate 59.4 s -> 45.0 s with the df64 kernel (unchanged output), 117.4 s
-> 103.8 s with the f64 kernel (same values as the CPU); profile 5.43 ->
4.03 us/pt. Needs siravan/symjit-utils#11 at a131443 or later (the reduction).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
